course: dictionary
lesson: 11972
title: Causative: the thing that makes it happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Causative» is a long, formal word, but it is built from a simple idea: cause, the reason something happens. A causative thing is the thing that makes another thing happen.
explain: «The strong wind was the causative factor in the broken window.» The wind made the window break, so the wind is the cause. Try swapping in a simpler phrase: «the reason for the broken window» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: In grammar, causative describes a sentence where someone makes something happen, or gets it done by someone else. «I had my hair cut» means I paid or asked someone to cut it. I did not cut it myself.
explain: Look for clue words: have, get, make and let. «She made him laugh» and «We got the car fixed» both use these clue words. Ask yourself: does someone else do the action for the subject? If yes, it is probably causative.
fact: Causative means causing something, or acting as its cause.
fact: «Causative» is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in science, health and grammar.
fact: A causative agent is the thing that causes a disease, such as a germ.
fact: «She made him laugh» and «I had my hair cut» are causative sentences: someone makes something happen, or has it done.
fact: Causative patterns often use have, get, make or let.
exercise: «The virus was the causative agent of the cold.» What does causative mean here? | Very quiet | *Causing the cold | Feeling sick after lunch | Cold and wet
exercise: «I had my bike repaired at the shop.» Did I fix the bike myself? | I broke it on purpose | I sold the bike | *No, someone else fixed it for me | Yes, I fixed it all alone
exercise: Which word is a clue for a causative sentence? | Blue | *Get | Under | Quickly
test: In «She made the dog sit», who makes the sitting happen? | The floor | *She | The dog | The sitting
test: «The causative factor of the flood was heavy rain.» What caused the flood? | The river bank | *Heavy rain | Summer holidays | Sunshine
exam: Which sentence is causative? | «The car drove fast.» | «The car was big.» | *«We got the car fixed.» | «The car is red.»
